-- title:
--   Theorem 5, p.26 — exchange alone generates $\mathfrak{su}(n_J)$ independently on every strong collective decoherence DFS
-- statement:
--   Let $n\ge 2$ qubits undergo strong collective decoherence. For a legal total spin $J$ and a legal magnetic number $m$, let $D=\mathrm{DFS}_n(J)$ at $m$, of dimension $n_J$, and let $H^n_J$ be the set of traceless Hermitian Hamiltonians $X$ obtained from exchange alone ($iX$ in the real Lie algebra generated by the $iE_{ab}$) that vanish on every spin sector other than $J$. Then $H^n_J$ acts as $\mathfrak{su}(n_J)$ on $D$:
--   1. every traceless Hermitian operator on $D$, extended by zero, agrees on $D$ with some $X\in H^n_J$;
--   2. every $X\in H^n_J$ agrees on $D$ with a traceless Hermitian operator on $D$, extended by zero; in particular it maps $D$ into itself.
--
--   Since each $X\in H^n_J$ vanishes off the spin-$J$ sector, these Hamiltonians act on this DFS only: exchange is universal on every DFS of strong collective decoherence, independently for each $J$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: acting as su(d_J) → su(n_J), n_J = dim DFS_n(J); reason: the proof works with su(n_J) on DFS_n(J) of dimension n_J (p.26); su(2J + 1) would be false since exchange commutes with the S_α
--   - reading: there exist sets H^n_J … acting independently on this DFS only → H^n_J := all traceless Hermitian X with iX in the closure and X = 0 off the spin-J sector; reason: the largest set with the printed properties; the theorem asserts it acts as su on the DFS
--   - generalization: Hamiltonians obtained by scalar multiplication, addition, Lie-commutator and unitary conjugation → i X in the real Lie algebra generated by the i E_ab (laws 1–3 only); reason: the smaller closure is contained in the printed one, so the Lean statement specializes to it; conjugation adds nothing (milestone (4.6))
--   - generalization: the DFS with m_J fixed; 'acting as su' read as reaching every su element → every legal m, and also clause 2 (every element of H^n_J acts on the DFS as an element of su); reason: both clauses at every m specialize to the printed claim at any fixed m
--   - encoding: half-integer labels J, m → doubled labels j2 = 2J : ℕ, m2 = 2m : ℤ; reason: exact half-integers; same instances
--   - encoding: qubits 1, …, n; |0⟩, |1⟩ → 0-based wires Fin n; Bool basis with false = |0⟩; reason: Lean convention; same operators
-- source:
--   Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, Theory of Decoherence-Free Fault-Tolerant Universal Quantum Computation, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, Theorem 5, §VII.D, p.26

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_IsSuOn
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_sectorSet
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_dfs
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_LegalJ
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_LegalM

open QAlgorithms

namespace CollectiveDFS

/-- Theorem 5 (Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, §VII.D, p.26, PDF p.26): "For any n ≥ 2 qubits undergoing strong collective
decoherence, there exist sets of Hamiltonians H^n_J obtained from exchange interactions only via
scalar multiplication, addition, Lie-commutator and unitary conjugation, acting as su(d_J) on the
DFS corresponding to the eigenvalue J. Furthermore each set acts independently on this DFS only
(i.e., with zeroes in the matrix representation corresponding to their action on the other
DFSs)."

Here `H^n_J = sectorSet n j2` is the set of traceless Hermitian `X` with `i X` in the real Lie
algebra generated by the exchanges and `X = 0` off the spin-`J` sector. For `n ≥ 2`, legal `J`
and legal `m`, with `D = DFS_n(J)` at `m`:
(a) every traceless Hermitian operator on `D` (extended by zero) agrees on `D` with some
`X ∈ H^n_J`;
(b) every `X ∈ H^n_J` agrees on `D` with some traceless Hermitian operator on `D` (extended by
zero); in particular `X` maps `D` into itself.

**Formalization Note** Doubled labels `j2 = 2J`, `m2 = 2m`; `d_J` is read as `n_J = dim DFS_n(J)`.
The closure omits unitary conjugation, which adds nothing (`CollectiveDFS.conj_mem_exchangeLie`);
scalars are real. `D` is the physical subspace of the `n`-qubit space, for every legal `m`. -/
theorem theorem_5 (n : ℕ) (hn : 2 ≤ n) (j2 : ℕ) (hJ : LegalJ n j2) (m2 : ℤ)
    (hm : LegalM j2 m2) :
    (∀ A : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ, IsSuOn (dfs n j2 m2) A →
      ∃ X ∈ sectorSet n j2, ∀ ψ ∈ dfs n j2 m2,
        Matrix.toEuclideanLin X ψ = Matrix.toEuclideanLin A ψ) ∧
    (∀ X ∈ sectorSet n j2, ∃ A : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ, IsSuOn (dfs n j2 m2) A ∧
      ∀ ψ ∈ dfs n j2 m2, Matrix.toEuclideanLin X ψ = Matrix.toEuclideanLin A ψ) := by sorry

end CollectiveDFS
